AB  - NutritionWise: A decoder nutrition label that is an artificial intelligence system that separates the complex information of food labels into easy tailored and practical information for the consumer. NutritionWise is a system that does not solely depend on the basic as is the case of the present systems raw data tracking or extraction, involves multimodal processing (image + text), retrieval- augmented generation (RAG) and large language models so as to provide context-sensitive explanations, health impact predictions and dietary suitability checks. The system uses TrOCR to do high-accuracy optical character recognition, LLaMA-3.2-1B and LLaMA-3-8B to do explanations and conversational support that are friendly to ordinary people, FAISS and SentenceTransformer to perform semantic retrieval and allergen matching. NutritionWise makes personal recommendations depending on databases such as the OpenFoodFacts and the WHO/FDA nutritional guidelines, smart notifications (e.g., high sodium, allergens), and nutrition plans depending on the individual health goals. Experimental analysis shows that the model presents high accuracy in text generation and text retrieval with a BLEU of 0.9758, ROUGE-L of 0.9871 and METEOR of 0.9923 that is almost human-like. A case study on the assessment of diabetic diets further helps to confirm their usefulness in a practical setting. NutritionWise is a large leap towards the right direction of offering customized nutrition counseling with a filter to t
