TI  - AI-Powered Mobile Web Application For Automated Dietary Tracking And Nutritional Analysis
AU  - niraj vaidya
AU  - Diwakar Rai
AU  - jaswant rao
PY  - 2026
JO  - Zenodo (CERN European Organization for Nuclear Research)
DO  - 10.5281/zenodo.20315433
UR  - https://openalex.org/W7161852836
LA  - en
AB  - This paper presents an AI-powered mobile web application for automated dietary tracking and nutritional analysis. The proposed system simplifies food logging using food image recognition, barcode scanning, and manual search features integrated with cloud-based synchronization. The application utilizes artificial intelligence models for food classification and retrieves nutritional data such as calories, proteins, carbohydrates, and fats from open food databases. Users can track daily calorie intake, monitor hydration levels, analyze macro nutrients, and view progress through interactive dashboards and analytics. The system is developed using Next.js, React.js, Firebase Firestore, Transformers.js, Open Food Facts API, and Recharts to provide a responsive and scalable dietary tracking solution. The study demonstrates how AI, cloud computing, and modern web technologies can improve user engagement and simplify nutrition monitoring and health management. Keywords: Artificial Intelligence, Dietary Tracking, Nutrition Analysis, Food Recognition, Health Technology, Web Application
