AB  - This study aims to design and develop an image recognition platform that analyzes nutrients from images of freshly cooked Thai dishes and automatically extracts their nutritional profiles based on the user’s location. Packaged foods are immediately recorded via the Open Food Facts API, retrieving complete nutritional information without additional training. Freshly cooked dishes are analyzed using a fine-tuned ResNet-50 model on the THFOOD-50 dataset (15,770 images, 50 classes), achieving an average accuracy of 78%, a precision of 79%, a recall of 77%, and F1-score of 77%. In addition, we design a database to store food items, nutrition facts, restaurant information, and geographic data from users, supporting a community-based approach. We also develop an intuitive mobile application that allows users to capture, review, and manage this information in real time. This platform enables people who need to monitor their diet, for example, those with NCD, obesity, or fitness goals, to make efficient decisions. The availability of comprehensive nutrition data holds significant potential to inform the formulation of evidence-based food policies by the Thai government, thereby contributing to future strategies aimed at improving public health outcomes.
