AB  - BioChain is a food trust scoring system built on blockchain technology that overcomes the weaknesses of existing centralized food authentication systems with trust through transparent, immutable, and low-cost food verification. BioChain leverages a multi-signal algorithm that assesses a trust score generating food trust scores based on five weighted measures certification verification$(30 \%)$, supply chain completeness$(25 \%)$, community feedback (20 %), price analysis (15 %), and AI-based risk assessment (10 %). BioChain processes information from various databases and application programming interfaces (APIs), including USDA FoodData Central and OpenFoodFacts. The BioChain application is constructed using a Polygon Amoy testnet which accommodates smart contract verification, with an average verification time of 2.8 seconds and transaction costs less than $0.01. The BioChain platform consists of a FastAPI backend, MetaMask, and a React frontend with QR scanning. The BioChain's scalability and dependability for transparent food authenticity verification are demonstrated by the experimental results of trust scores, which range from 51 to 98 %. The mean trust scores for organic brands are higher.
