AB  - The rapid growth of processed and packaged foods has created challenges for consumers attempting to make informed dietary choices. Interpreting detailed traditional labels is often very complex and consumes lots of time, leading to poor dietary decisions and associated health complications. This paper reviews NutriGrade ML, a smart packaged food assessment system, that uses barcode scanning and machine learning to evaluate the nutritional quality of packaged products. The system integrates the pyNutriScore python with cosine similarity-based recommendation algorithms that calculates the NutriGrade of packaged food and suggests alternatives. By retrieving product information from Open Food Facts API, the system computes NutriScore grades, detects potential allergens and suggests healthier substitutes with same product category. The recommendation engine applies TFIDF vectorization on ingredients and product text to identify nutritionally superior alternatives. This review analyzes the system’s architecture, machine learning components and comparative performance against existing food analysis applications. NutriGrade ML will simplify nutritional decision making, enhance transparency in food labeling and support healthier consumer choices.
