AB  - The trend of consuming packaged food products is on the rise. However, it has posed a challenge to the consumers to take a wise decision while choosing a food product. It may require a lot of time to comprehend the intricacies of the traditional nutritional label found on the food product. This may lead to a poor decision regarding the food product, which may cause health-related problems for the consumer. The paper proposes a system called NutriGrade ML that utilizes a barcode scanning method along with a machine learning algorithm to assess the nutritional quality of the packaged food product. The proposed system utilizes a library called pyNutriScore along with a recommendation engine that utilizes a cosine similarity algorithm to calculate the NutriGrade of the food product. The system retrieves the information related to the food product by using the Open Food Facts API. The Open Food Facts API is an open-source food product database that contains over 4 million food products that are accessible worldwide. The NutriScore is computed by utilizing the pyNutriScore library. The NutriGrade is computed by utilizing the functions provided by the library. The system recommends a healthy food product by utilizing the TF-IDF method and cosine similarity algorithm. The efficiency of the system is validated by utilizing the experimental results for various parameters, such as average cosine similarity for top-N recommendations, precision@3 for recommendation quality, average NutriS
