AB  - Food composition activities include sampling and sample preparation, data generation, data compilation, data dissemination and data use. Food composition data are useful, mainly in health, agriculture, environment and trade (including the food industry) sectors. This chapter discusses the various food composition activities of organizations at the international, national, and regional levels, and focuses on the technical elements used for analyzing food composition data. It provides an overview of analytical methods commonly used for macronutrients, along with their applications and limitations. It also discusses the commonly measured food components, their recommended units of measure for most food composition purposes, and International Network of Food Data Systems (INFOODS) tagnames, the use of which will minimise misinterpretation of the food component. Even with appropriate metadata, there will still be limitations in all food composition databases.
