AB  - Biological rhythms are cycles that operate accordingto the light and dark phase. Humans and animals continue theirmetabolic activities in 24-hour biorhythms known as diurnaland nocturnal. It is thought that biorhythms can change the effectsof nutrients as well as many effects, and also, in some cases,nutrients can direct biological rhythms. This situation makes itnecessary to embody the interaction of biorhythms and metabolism.In the last 50 years, there has been a period in whichfood understanding, nutrition style and food technologies arerapidly developing and changing. Approaches such as functionalfoods, hyper-nutrients, antioxidants, phytochemicals andprobiotics have changed classical approaches to food. The relationshipbetween biological rhythms and bioactive nutrients infoods also draws attention as a new approach. Biorhythms, physiologicalcycles, metabolism and nutrient relationships, functionalizingfoods and using them as drugs, targeted utilization ofbioactive nutrients have become the goals of scientific studies.Although the knowledge of biorhythms and the therapeutic useof plants goes back to ancient times, scientific studies are new.Bio-active nutritional components such as polyphenols affectthe biological clock through signaling pathways, while biorhythmsand nutrients can shape each other’s effect, for example,a correct breakfast is thought to positively affect the biorhythmclock. Functional foods and bioactive nutrients can prevent chroniccases such as obesity a
